{"notes": "The labour market is softening modestly but not acutely. Unemployment has ticked up to 3.7% from a 3.6% trough, but the 3m change is flat and the 12m change is only -0.1pp. The Sahm gap sits at 3bps—well below recession thresholds—and the rate remains 0.3pp below the estimated natural rate. There is slack emerging, but it is neither sharp nor sudden. Inflation has cooled further but remains above target. Headline CPI stands at 1.83% yoy, down 0.17pp over three months, while core PCE is 1.64% yoy, essentially flat at the margin. The 3m annualized core rate is 1.61%, and headline momentum is 0.18% mpm. Both are contained, though headline momentum is still slightly elevated on a multi-month view. Financial conditions remain accommodative—the NFCI is -0.58, essentially unchanged on a 4w view, well below zero, and the market is pricing in significant near-term easing.

