ort a near-term pause. Flatten front-end curve by shorting 6m (where hike-cut expectations cluster) and holding 2y—a bet on rate peak and policy patience."}}

{"notes": "Labor markets show creeping looseness despite very tight near-term backdrop. The unemployment rate has drifted upward over the past three months (+10bps), even as the 12-month trend points lower. The Sahm rule at +10bps and the rate 40bps below the natural rate imply slack is opening incrementally. This contradicts the impression of extreme tightness: the rate is now at the center of its recent range, not its low, and the range has widened. The one-month-ahead horizon gives little time for momentum to reverse, but the direction is softening.

